.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt LEGION 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm legion
.Nd container and VM orchestrator, image builder, and local jail runner for FreeBSD
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -server Ar host:port
.Op Fl -identity Ar path
.Ar command
.Op Ar args ...
.Nm
.Cm build
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar context
.Nm
.Cm build vm
.Op Fl t Ar name Ns Op : Ns Ar tag
.Fl -disk Ar path | Fl -rootfs Ar dir Op Fl -size Ar size
.Nm
.Cm local
.Op Ar local-options
.Ar subcommand
.Op Ar args ...
.Nm
.Fl V | -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a container and virtual-machine orchestrator for
.Fx
built on jails,
VNET,
.Xr pf 4 ,
.Xr rctl 8 ,
.Xr bhyve 8 ,
and ZFS.
A single binary provides the node daemon
.Pq Nm Cm daemon ,
the cluster CLI, the native OCI image builder
.Pq Nm Cm build ,
and the standalone local jail/VM runner
.Pq Nm Cm local .
.Sh GLOBAL OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -server Ar host:port
Manager gRPC endpoint.
Overrides
.Ev LEGION_SERVER
and defaults to
.Li 127.0.0.1:7470 .
.It Fl -identity Ar path
PEM file holding the client certificate, private key, and cluster CA.
Overrides
.Ev LEGION_IDENTITY
and defaults to
.Pa /var/db/legion/admin.pem .
.It Fl h , -help
Print usage information.
.It Fl V , -version
Print version information.
.El
.Sh CLUSTER AND NODE COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm daemon Op Ar options
Run the node daemon (manager and, on
.Fx ,
worker agent).
Key options include
.Fl -data-dir ,
.Fl -run-dir ,
.Fl -listen ,
.Fl -advertise ,
.Fl -no-agent ,
.Fl -node-name ,
.Fl -zfs-root ,
.Fl -linux ,
.Fl -metrics-listen ,
.Fl -console-listen ,
.Fl -ingress-listen ,
.Fl -ingress-tls-listen ,
.Fl -insecure-registry ,
.Fl -builder ,
.Fl -builder-arg ,
.Fl -iscsi-targets ,
.Fl -iscsi-portal-group ,
and
.Fl -iscsi-portal .
A builder node runs Builds with
.Fl -builder ,
by default this binary as
.Nm Cm local .
.It Cm init
Initialize a new cluster with the reached manager as its first member.
.It Cm join-token Ar manager|worker Op Fl -rotate
Print or rotate the cluster join token for the given role.
.It Cm join Ar token Fl -manager Ar host:port Op Ar options
Join an existing cluster before starting the daemon.
.It Cm status
Show the reached manager's view of the cluster.
.It Cm doctor Oo Fl -zfs-root Ar dataset Oc Oo Fl -json Oc
Check whether this host meets Legion's requirements without making changes.
.It Cm diagnose Oo Fl -node Ar name Oc Oo Fl -json Oc
Run
.Cm doctor
checks across cluster nodes.
.It Cm support-bundle Op Fl o Ar file
Export a masked cluster diagnostics bundle.
.It Cm backup Fl o Ar file
Save a consistent snapshot of all cluster objects.
.It Cm restore Op Ar file
Restore a stopped manager's store from a backup or its own store.
.It Cm autolock Ar enable|disable|rotate|show
Manage manager key sealing; restarted sealed managers wait for
.Cm unlock .
.It Cm unlock Op Fl -key-file Ar path
Provide the unlock key to a sealed manager on this host.
.It Cm ca Ar rotate|status
Rotate the cluster CA or inspect rotation progress.
.It Cm console Ar login|settings|configure|oidc
Generate a one-time web console sign-in URL, or view/configure console
settings and OIDC.
.It Cm user create Ar name Oo Fl -role Ar view|edit|admin Fl n Ar ns Oc Oo Fl o Ar file Oc
Create a user client certificate PEM and optional
.Li RoleBinding .
.It Cm node Ar drain|pause|activate|promote|demote|label|require
Manage node availability, manager role, labels, and host readiness requirements.
.Cm node drain ,
.Cm volume move
and
.Cm delete
of a node or a Service first ask the leader what the change would do:
the Volumes that move and their sizes, work no node would take, a Volume
left behind, a node without room for what moves there, data lost with a
node still up, and what a disruption budget holds back.
A change that would not complete is refused unless
.Fl -force
is given;
.Fl -dry-run
prints the check, changes nothing, and exits 1 if anything blocks.
.El
.Sh WORKLOAD AND OBSERVABILITY COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm apply Fl f Ar file|-
Create or update objects from YAML or JSON.
.It Cm diff Fl f Ar file|-
Preview changes
.Cm apply
would make; exits 1 if differences exist.
.It Cm get Ar kind name Oo Fl n Ar ns Oc Oo Fl o Ar yaml|json Oc
Show a single object.
.It Cm list Ar kind Oo Fl n Ar ns | Fl A Oc Oo Fl l Ar selector Oc Oo Fl o Ar fmt Oc
List objects of a kind.
.It Cm delete Ar kind name Oo Fl n Ar ns Oc Op Fl -dry-run | Fl -force
Delete an object.
A node's removal and a Service's deletion are checked first, as
.Cm node drain
is.
.It Cm watch Oo Ar kind Oc Oo Fl -from Ar version Oc
Stream live object changes, from now on or after a version.
.It Cm stack Ar deploy|convert|ls|stop|start|rm
Deploy, inspect, stop, start, or remove Compose stacks.
.It Cm stop Ar service , Cm start Ar service
Stop a service while keeping its spec, or start it again.
.It Cm pause Ar service , Cm resume Ar service
Freeze a service's tasks where they run, out of its endpoints and their
probes held, or let them go on.
.It Cm restart Ar service , Cm rollback Ar service
Trigger a rolling restart or roll back a service to its previous spec.
.It Cm cronjob run Ar name Op Fl n Ar ns
Run a CronJob immediately outside its schedule.
.It Cm top Oo Fl n Ar ns Oc Oo Fl -once Oc
Open the live terminal dashboard.
.It Cm logs Ar task|service Oo Fl c Ar container Oc Oo Fl f Oc Oo Fl -tail Ar n Oc
Print or follow container logs.
.It Cm build-logs Ar build Oo Fl n Ar ns Oc Oo Fl f Oc
Print or follow a Build's output.
.It Cm logs-search Ar service|job Oo Fl -since Ar dur Oc Oo Fl -until Ar dur Oc Oo Ar text Oc
Search logs across a Service's or Job's tasks.
.It Cm exec Ar task|service Oo Fl c Ar container Oc Oo Fl i Oc Oo Fl t Oc -- Ar cmd ...
Run a command inside a running task's container.
.It Cm files Ar task|service Op Ar path , Cm cp Ar src dest
List or copy files inside a task's container root.
.It Cm port-forward Ar task|service Ar port ...
Forward local ports to a task's pod.
.It Cm events Oo Ar kind/name Oc Oo Fl n Ar ns Oc Oo Fl w Oc
Show or follow recent cluster events.
.It Cm activity Oo Ar id|name Oc Oo Fl w Oc Oo Fl o Ar fmt Oc
Show or follow long operations: drains, Volume moves, restores and
replicas' whole copies, each with its stage, the bytes sent and how it
ended; with an id, its stages and full output.
.It Cm alerts Oo Fl n Ar ns Oc Oo Fl w Oc Oo Fl o Ar fmt Oc
Show active cluster alerts.
.It Cm usage Op Fl n Ar ns , Cm quota Op Fl n Ar ns
Inspect task resource usage samples and namespace quotas.
.It Cm audit Op Ar options
Query the cluster audit trail (cluster admin only).
.It Cm reach Op Fl n Ar ns , Cm load-balancers Op Fl n Ar ns
Evaluate NetworkPolicy reachability or show CARP load balancer holders.
.It Cm volume Ar move|backup|restore|snapshots|snapshot|rollback|rm-snapshot
Manage persistent volumes and ZFS snapshots.
.It Cm image Ar load|ls|pull|push|rm|prune|scan|export|search|sbom|inspect
Manage cached images on cluster nodes, inspect registries, and run
.Fx
.Cm pkg audit
vulnerability scans.
.El
.Sh BUILD COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm build Oo Ar options Oc Oo Ar context Oc , Cm build jail Oo Ar options Oc Oo Ar context Oc
Build a
.Fx
OCI image from a
.Pa Containerfile
using native jails (or
.Fl -backend Cm buildah ) .
.It Cm build vm Oo Fl t Ar name Ns Oo : Ns Ar tag Oc Oc Fl -disk Ar path | Fl -rootfs Ar dir Oo Fl -size Ar size Oc
Package a raw disk image or
.Fx
rootfs directory (via
.Xr makefs 8 )
into an OCI image containing
.Pa /disk.img
for
.Xr bhyve 8 .
The store options
.Fl -state-dir ,
.Fl -zfs-root
and
.Fl -no-zfs
may come before
.Cm vm
or after it.
.El
.Sh LOCAL COMMANDS
.Nm Cm local
runs standalone image, build, signing, and container operations on the local
host without a cluster daemon.
Local global options are
.Fl -state-dir ,
.Fl -zfs-root ,
.Fl -no-zfs ,
.Fl -pod-subnet ,
and
.Fl -plain-http .
Subcommands:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm init , build , check , doctor , login
Scaffold a
.Pa Containerfile ,
build images, check Legion compatibility, inspect host readiness, and save
registry credentials.
.It Cm run Oo Ar options Oc Oo Ar image Oc Oo Ar cmd ... Oc
Run an image in a local
.Fx
jail
.Pq Fl -vnet , Fl p , Fl v , Fl e , Fl -linux
or as a local
.Xr bhyve 8
virtual machine
.Pq Fl -vm , Fl -vm-cpus , Fl -vm-memory , Fl -vm-boot Cm bhyveload|uefi .
.It Cm ps , logs , exec , stop , rm
List, inspect logs, exec into, stop, and remove local containers.
.It Cm pull , load , push , export , images , rmi , prune
Manage the local OCI image store and registries.
.It Cm publish , manifest
Build across multiple platform hosts and push multi-architecture OCI indexes.
.It Cm sign , verify , attest , sbom , key
Create signing keys, sign manifests, and attach or inspect SLSA provenance
and SPDX SBOM attestations.
.El
.Pp
Pods
.Pq Cm run Fl -vnet , Fl p
are on the bridge
.Li legionlocal0 ;
their published ports are
.Xr pf 4
rules in anchors under
.Li legion-local/ ,
which
.Pa /etc/pf.conf
must call before its filter rules:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
nat-anchor "legion-local/*"
rdr-anchor "legion-local/*"
anchor "legion-local/*"
.Ed
.Pp
With neither
.Fl -state-dir
nor
.Fl -zfs-root
given, the first
.Nm Cm local
command moves the state of the former standalone jailer,
.Pa /var/db/jailer
and
.Li zroot/jailer ,
to
.Pa /var/db/legion-local
and
.Li zroot/legion-local ,
unless it still holds containers.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev LEGION_SERVER
Default manager address for
.Fl -server .
.It Ev LEGION_IDENTITY
Default client credentials PEM path for
.Fl -identity .
.It Ev LEGION_LOCAL_STATE_DIR , LEGION_LOCAL_ZFS_ROOT , LEGION_LOCAL_NO_ZFS , LEGION_LOCAL_POD_SUBNET , LEGION_LOCAL_CACHE_MAX , LEGION_LOCAL_SSH
Defaults for local store and build options under
.Cm build
and
.Cm local .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/db/legion/
Default daemon data directory and
.Pa admin.pem
location.
.It Pa /var/run/legion/
Default daemon runtime directory.
.It Pa /var/db/legion-local/
Default
.Nm Cm local
state directory, run as root; otherwise
.Pa ~/.local/share/legion-local/ .
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d/legion
.Fx
.Xr rc 8
service script.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Start a single-node cluster with the web console enabled:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
service legion start
legion init
legion console login
.Ed
.Pp
Build a jail image and a bhyve VM image locally:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
legion build -t myapp:1 .
legion build vm -t myvm:1 --rootfs ./guest-root --size 512m
legion local run --rm --vm --vm-memory 512m localhost/myvm:1
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pf 4 ,
.Xr bhyve 8 ,
.Xr jail 8 ,
.Xr makefs 8 ,
.Xr rctl 8 ,
.Xr zfs 8
